      "id": "capo-logic-for-guitar-and-mandolin",
      "title": "Capo Logic for Guitar and Mandolin",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** transposition | **Difficulty:** 3/10 | **Time:** ~8 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A capo raises pitch without changing chord shapes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "how-it-works",
      "title": "How it works",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "G shapes + capo 2 = A major. Capo 3 from G = B♭. Capo 5 from G = C. Each fret = one semitone."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "why-use-it",
      "title": "Why use it",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Open-chord resonance and easier fingerings in keys that would otherwise require barre chords. Balance against vocal range."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "communication",
      "title": "Communication",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Tell the band 'capo 2, G shapes in A' to avoid mismatch with concert-pitch instruments."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
